          Practical topics for choosing fence systems, accessories, surface finishes, packing methods, and repeat-order
          details.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section blog" aria-label="Blog articles">
        <div class="blog-grid">
          <article>
            <span>Guide</span>
            <h3>How to choose temporary fence feet for different sites</h3>
            <p>Compare concrete, recycled plastic, and blow-molded bases for stability, cost, and container space.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>Finish</span>
            <h3>Hot-dip galvanized or powder coated fence panels?</h3>
            <p>Match coating choice to corrosion resistance, appearance, market preference, and project budget.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>Packing</span>
            <h3>What to confirm before fence container loading</h3>
            <p>Check panel bundles, accessory cartons, pallet design, labels, and loading sequence before shipment.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>Accessories</span>
            <h3>Why fence accessories should be confirmed with panels</h3>
            <p>Feet, clamps, stays, hinges, latches, and gates affect site installation speed and order completeness.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>Projects</span>
            <h3>How to prepare a fence inquiry for faster quotation</h3>
            <p>Send drawings, panel size, finish, quantity, packing preference, and destination port to reduce back-and-forth.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>Buying</span>
            <h3>Standard fence products vs custom OEM production</h3>
            <p>Understand when to choose common market dimensions and when custom fabrication makes better sense.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
